<h2>Why there is no form</h2>

<p>
    A contact form on a static site has to post somewhere, which means either a third-party
    endpoint or an API key sitting in client-side JavaScript. The previous version of this site had
    the latter. A form would also be the only third-party request on the entire site, and the
    performance budget in CI sets third-party requests to zero — not as a target but as a
    constraint, so that a convenience cannot quietly reintroduce one.
</p>

<p>
    A <code>mailto:</code> link does the same job with no key to leak and nothing to maintain.
</p>

<h2>If something here is wrong</h2>

<p>
    Tell me. Every number on this site carries a recorded basis and a date, and several are marked
    approximate or projected because that is what the evidence supports. If one of them does not
    survive contact with your reading of it, I would rather hear that than not.
</p>
